    "otherOrganization": "xRegistry project",
    "introduction": [
      "A machine that carries an AI model has to answer questions no existing OPC UA specification asks. Which model is running, where does it run, what was it trained on, who approved it for this line, and what happens when the link to the place it runs goes away. A Client can discover a robot's construction in detail and cannot discover the model deciding what the robot does.",
      "The model itself is rarely the hard part. Runtimes to execute one are plentiful and interchangeable, and a payload is a tensor or a document either way. What is missing is the description: a common way to say that this deployment serves that version of that model, trained on that dataset, evaluated with that result, and reachable at that endpoint until it is not.",
      "This document defines that description as an OPC UA information model. Models, datasets, deployments and jobs become browseable Objects with stable identity and provenance, so an operator asks what produced a decision and gets an answer from the same Services already used to read a temperature."
    ],
    "draftBanner": "PROVISIONAL WORKING DRAFT — not normative, not endorsed by the OPC Foundation. The document number, the Mantis project identifier and every NodeId in this document are placeholders; the OPC Foundation assigns the real values."
  },
